  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AI Governance and Regulation Workshop</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A 1.5 day training workshop in Danang for 65 participants including National Assembly deputies and members of local people&#x2019;s council in second week of December to discuss AI governance and regulation. The UK experts &#x2013; joining in person or virtually - will present about the UK&#x2019;s approach in AI regulations and governance, how the UK developed it and its impacts on industry as well as international trends and practice in some other countries. Other speakers will be from UN agencies and Vietnamese organisation or UN agency etc providing facts and figures on AI&#x2019;s impact on certain issues.  

If the UK expert is able to travel to Vietnam for the workshop, an extended discussion between the Embassy and the Committee of Science, Technology and Environment of the National Assembly will be organised in Hanoi to build a stronger connection and try to shape their early thinking on AI regulations. If time and budget allows, another meeting with researchers of Ho Chi Minh National Political Academy (as a key Party body to influence) to share UK experiences on AI governance and regulation will be organised.</narrative>
  </description>
